{"name":"Forbidden Fruit","hex":"#fe7b7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forbidden fruit","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit forbidden to Adam.","Illicit pleasure."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forbidden_fruit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hoegaarden Brewery","blocks":[{"text":"Hoegaarden Brewery is a brewery in Hoegaarden, Belgium, and the producer of a witbier, a type of wheat beer. Hoegaarden de-emphasizes hops, and is unfiltered, giving it the hazy, or milky, appearance--which makes it a wit (white) beer."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoegaarden_Brewery"},{"title":"Forbidden Fruit (liqueur)","blocks":[{"text":"Forbidden Fruit was a 27.9-40% ABV grapefruit liqueur first created in the late 1800s and manufactured by Charles Jacquin et Cie. It was significant in pre-Prohibition cocktail recipes and continued being used frequently after the repeal of Prohibition in the United States. It ceased production in the late 1970s as its classic spherical bottle design was used for the then new Chambord."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbidden_Fruit_(liqueur)"},{"title":"Forbidden fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In Abrahamic religions, forbidden fruit is a name given to the fruit growing in the Garden of Eden that God commands mankind not to eat. In the Biblical story of Genesis, Adam and Eve disobey God and commit the original sin, eating the forbidden fruit from the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, and are exiled from Eden:"},{"text":"And the Lord God commanded the man, saying, Of every tree of the garden thou mayest freely eat:"},{"text":"But of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, thou shalt not eat of it: for in the day that thou eatest thereof thou shalt surely die."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg/330px-Jan_Brueghel_de_Oude_en_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Het_aards_paradijs_met_de_zondeval_van_Adam_en_Eva.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbidden_fruit"},{"title":"Fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fruit is the seed-bearing structure in flowering plants (angiosperms) that is formed from the ovary after flowering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg/330px-Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg/500px-Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg/1280px-Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg/500px-Hoegaarden_Wit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of Hoegaarden wheat beer in its iconic hexagonal glass, served alongside the beer bottle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoegaarden_Wit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Hoegaarden_-_Verboden_Vrucht_and_glass.jpg/500px-Hoegaarden_-_Verboden_Vrucht_and_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Hoegaarden_-_Verboden_Vrucht_and_glass.jpg/500px-Hoegaarden_-_Verboden_Vrucht_and_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Forbidden fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoegaarden_-_Verboden_Vrucht_and_glass.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Plaincourault_fresco%2C_Garde